    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0590" n="578" xml:id="pg578"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24546/11: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-22T19:00:00+01:00">October 22, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—2:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5045. Regarding your 4458, October 15, 7 p.m. and your 4564, October 20, 1
                        p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d567-f1"/> Eden told me this evening that His
                    Majesty’s Government agreed in principle and that they would give me a
                    memorandum on specific questions of detail tomorrow. This is the third time that
                    I have pressed this matter. Several Ministries are concerned and the Foreign
                    Office has not yet been able to obtain complete clearance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
